  "curated_api_module": "ugence_agent_value_readiness.api",
  "note": "Machine-readable snapshot of the curated public API. Generated from the installed package; tests/packaging/test_public_api.py asserts equality. ReadinessTarget/RequirementClass are reused from ugence-uvi-policy-contracts. GateResult embeds a PolicyGate (kind/applicability derived, not caller-set); blocking/indeterminate gate ids are derived properties of the determination, not fields. GV-3R-b adds the single canonical evaluator entry point evaluate_readiness(case, *, evaluation_time): ReadinessEvaluationCase carries NO classification field — the evaluator selects the tier — and ReadinessEvaluationResult is advisory, never a deployment authorization. Readiness requirements are policy/gate-driven: indicator records are diagnostics, not a global prerequisite. The governing ReadinessPolicy's lifecycle state and effective period are evaluated as ADR §6 precondition row 0 at the explicit evaluation_time. Trusted Readiness Orchestration adds the single canonical boundary assess_readiness(request, *, policy_resolver, gate_verifier, condition_verifier) around that one evaluator — no second classification algorithm exists and no new readiness classification is defined. M-3R.3 adds the Intelligence/Capability/Adoption indicator catalogs and wires the AssessedSystemBinding through that SAME single entry point. OWNERSHIP (UVI ADR §20): AssessedSystemBinding, SystemBindingAuthenticityStatus and SystemIdentityContractError are OWNED BY ugence-governance-contracts (>=0.3.0) and are DIRECT RE-EXPORTS here — readiness_api.AssessedSystemBinding IS governance_api.AssessedSystemBinding, so exactly one class identity, one canonical serialization and one digest exist; this package holds no copy, subclass, adapter or parallel schema. Readiness owns the indicator catalogs, the admission rules, the binding-to-AssessmentContext adapter, the orchestration gap codes and the trace. Behaviourally: assess_readiness now REQUIRES an exact AssessedSystemBinding (a missing one is NOT_EVALUATED, never a headline) and admits only catalog-recognized, system-bound indicator results into the sanitized case. READINESS_ORCHESTRATOR_VERSION therefore advances to ugence.readiness-orchestration/v0.2 while EVALUATOR_FORMULA_VERSION stays exactly GV-3R-b.3 — the classification algorithm did not move. There is no legacy unbound entry point. A catalog defines governed VOCABULARY, never a requirement: binding an Intelligence, Capability or Adoption catalog makes no family globally mandatory, and catalog membership is NOT evidence verification — a result's MetricClaim axes are carried through unchanged. AssessedSystemBinding is STRUCTURAL: its authenticity_status is a permanently STRUCTURAL_UNVERIFIED property and authenticity_verified a permanently-False property, because no ratified system-binding verifier exists; SystemManifest and the RA-owned SubjectContext are referenced by opaque ref + digest and are NOT minted here. No Benchmark Registry, no evidence/TAP verification, no condition enforcement, no forecasting and no financial or ROI vocabulary is introduced. READINESS_ORCHESTRATOR_VERSION is platform-neutral and names no milestone; every ReadinessTrustGapCode value carries the neutral READINESS_ORCHESTRATION_ namespace, which likewise names no milestone. Every injected boundary defaults to None, which DENIES: the exact ReadinessPolicy must resolve through the shared Ugence Policy Authority's public resolution service, and only independently verified gate results and conditions reach the evaluator. ReadinessAssessmentRequest carries no classification, no trust boolean, no policy body and no financial field; ReadinessAssessmentOutcome is advisory, unsigned, and authorizes_deployment is a permanently-False property, not a field. No allow-all or testing verifier is exported — that absence is the boundary.",
